<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Healthy Minds for Healthy Bodies – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Scenario:</b> Checking in on Health</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Theme:</b> Healthy Minds for Healthy Bodies</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Outline strategies for personal development. Interactive: Create a study guide, collaboratively, on various topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can outline strategies for personal development related to health and balance in a well-organized text (e.g., "To maintain a healthy lifestyle, I plan to exercise three times a week using a tracker, eat balanced meals, and practice mindfulness daily.")
            Can collaboratively create a study guide on health and wellness topics, incorporating tips and strategies (e.g., "Include sections on stress management techniques, like deep breathing exercises and time management tips.")
            Can write reflections on personal habits and suggest improvements by using health technology to achieve better life balance (e.g., "I have been staying up too late, so I use a sleep tracker to set a better bedtime routine.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%; text-align: left;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 34%; text-align: left;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%; text-align: left;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of images depicting various health technologies and practices (e.g., a smartwatch tracking activity, someone meditating with an app, a healthy meal prep, a sleep tracker graph). Students are given a minute to write down 3-5 keywords or short phrases associated with "healthy minds and bodies" inspired by the images, focusing on strategies and tools. They share one idea in small groups.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a short reflective statement on the board, modeling the use of Present Perfect Continuous and a modal for possibility, for example: "I <b>have been</b> trying to improve my hydration by using a water <b>tracker</b> app. You <b>might need</b> to drink more water during the day if you want to boost your energy." The teacher highlights the target grammar and vocabulary (e.g., <b>tracker, hydration, boost, energy</b>), practicing the /b/ sound in "boost" and "balance" as well as sentence rhythm.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'I have been trying,' does that mean I finished trying or I'm still doing it?" (Expected answer: Still doing it.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'You might need to drink more water,' am I giving a command or a suggestion?" (Expected answer: A suggestion/recommendation.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Checking in on Health".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students are provided with a short blog post titled "Top 5 Strategies for a Balanced Digital Life" or an excerpt from an online article about using health technology for well-being. The text outlines strategies for personal development, stress management, and maintaining a healthy lifestyle, incorporating specific vocabulary (e.g., <b>mindfulness, self-care, routine, sleep pattern, activity level, consistent</b>) and grammatical structures (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, Modals for possibility).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> The students will interpret written information about health strategies to prepare for outlining their own development plans and collaboratively creating a study guide.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the blog post silently.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is the main purpose of this article?" (e.g., To recommend strategies for a healthier lifestyle using technology.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match sections of the article to headings like "Managing Stress," "Improving Sleep," and "Boosting Physical Activity."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students identify and underline sentences in the text that use the Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, or Modals for possibility.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice writing sentences using the Present Perfect Continuous for ongoing health efforts, the Second Conditional for hypothetical well-being improvements, and Modals for possibility to suggest health strategies. They will incorporate target vocabulary such as <b>hydration, mindfulness, balance, routine, stress, tracker, self-care</b>, and verbs like <b>exercise, practice, manage, monitor</b>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> Students complete sentences using the correct form of the verb in parentheses and appropriate vocabulary from a word bank.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I ______ (practice) ______ (meditation) to manage ______ for months." (e.g., have been practicing mindfulness, stress)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I ______ (track) my ______ (sleep pattern) more consistently, I ______ (feel) more ______ (energized)." (e.g., tracked, would feel)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"You ______ (consider) using a ______ (tracker) to ______ (monitor) your ______ (activity level)." (e.g., might/could, activity)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled (Sentence Transformation):</b> Students rewrite sentences, changing the grammatical structure or incorporating specific vocabulary words provided.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I started exercising daily last month and I'm still doing it." -> Rewrite using Present Perfect Continuous and 'fitness'. (e.g., "I <b>have been exercising</b> daily to improve my <b>fitness</b>.")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"It's possible that deep breathing exercises could reduce stress." -> Rewrite using a modal for possibility and 'mindfulness'. (e.g., "You <b>could try mindfulness</b> exercises to reduce <b>stress</b>.")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I don't have enough time to join a yoga class, so I'm not doing it." -> Rewrite using Second Conditional and 'flexibility'. (e.g., "If I <b>had</b> more free time, I <b>would join</b> a yoga class to increase my <b>flexibility</b>.")</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Writing & Peer Check:</b> In pairs, students write two original sentences for each target grammar structure (PPC, 2nd Conditional, Modals for possibility), focusing on health and well-being. They then exchange their sentences with another pair and provide feedback on grammar accuracy and vocabulary usage. (Pragmatic: Giving health suggestions in a polite tone).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Checking in on Health".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: Collaborative Study Guide Section.</b> Students work in groups of 3-4 to collaboratively write a section for a "Healthy Minds for Healthy Bodies" study guide. Each group will choose one aspect of well-being (e.g., Stress Management, Hydration and Nutrition, Sleep and Rest, Physical Activity, Digital Detox) and outline 3-4 practical strategies for personal development related to it, incorporating the use of health technology. They must use each of the target grammar structures (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, Modals for possibility) at least once in their written section. They should also embed at least five of the target vocabulary words (e.g., <b>balance, routine, self-care, app, feedback, restorative, consistent</b>).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Instructions for students:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Choose a topic for your study guide section (e.g., "Stress Management for Students").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Brainstorm 3-4 strategies related to your topic. Consider how health technology can support these strategies.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Write your section, ensuring it is well-organized and clearly outlines the strategies.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">You must include at least one sentence using the Present Perfect Continuous (e.g., "I have been practicing mindfulness daily to reduce stress."), one using the Second Conditional (e.g., "If I managed my screen time better, I would improve my sleep quality."), and one using Modals for possibility (e.g., "You might want to try a meditation app for daily self-care.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integrate at least five new vocabulary words from our list.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ensure your tone is polite and respectful when giving suggestions, using formal expressions where appropriate (Sociolinguistic).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Groups submit their collaboratively written section of the "Healthy Living Study Guide."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment: Peer-Assessment Checklist and Teacher Observation.</b> Students will peer-assess another group's study guide section using a simple checklist provided by the teacher, focusing on the following criteria. The teacher will circulate and observe group collaboration and writing process.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Peer-Assessment Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and organization of strategies (Are the strategies easy to understand?).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of Present Perfect Continuous (Is it used to describe ongoing efforts?).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of Second Conditional (Is it used for hypothetical improvements?).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of Modals for possibility (Are suggestions given politely?).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integration of at least five target vocabulary words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate tone (polite and respectful when discussing health).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following prompts individually:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new vocabulary word I used effectively in my writing today is ______ because ______."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did collaborating with my group help me to outline health strategies more effectively?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Connecting learning and planning next steps.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing a clear outline for health strategies did I find most challenging today, and what could I do to improve next time?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can the strategies discussed and outlined today help me make conscious efforts to improve my personal well-being or help others check in on their health?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well during this writing lesson? (e.g., Student engagement in collaborative writing, successful application of the Second Conditional).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students to further improve their written production of health strategies and reflections? (e.g., More sentence starters for Present Perfect Continuous, additional practice distinguishing between 'might' and 'could').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How will this lesson connect to the next lesson (Mediation & Integration)? (The collaboratively written study guide sections will form the basis for a larger project or presentation where students will mediate information about health and wellness to a broader audience.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>